{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792423616,"nonce":"vs04RoRlhQ+4q9KqtoWvtoBLAeg=","title":"A GPU error in a frame ended the program, and a canvas could ask for a texture past the device's limit","message":"RayDE stopped with an uncaught exception from `Renderer.failOnError`:\n\n    gpu error drawing: Validation Error\n      In Device::create_texture\n        Dimension Y value 14523 exceeds the limit of 8192\n\n**What happened**\n\n`failOnError` threw on every error the device reported after a frame was submitted, and `WindowedApp.run` rethrows, so any validation error closed the window. Where the error came from is not in the report: wgpu reports it on the device after the fact, with no name for the texture.\n\nA canvas's triangles live in one texture, `ROW_TEXELS` wide and as many rows as it needs, grown by half again each time. 14523 is `needed + needed / 2` for 9682 rows, so the canvas's table is the likely texture; it had no bound, and the growth could pass the limit even when the rows needed did not. Mesh textures took their image's size as it was.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- A device asks for the adapter's largest texture side, not the 8192 a device gets unasked (16384 on this Mac); `Renderer.maxTexture` holds it.\n- A canvas's table stops taking triangles at three quarters of that many rows, keeping the rest for clips, and says so once on stderr; a canvas whose clips overrun it draws no paths. The growth is clamped to the limit.\n- A mesh texture larger than the limit is shrunk to it.\n- `Renderer.strict` (`Offscreen.strictErrors`): on, as for tests and tools, a GPU error in a frame throws; off, as `WindowedApp` sets it, the error is written once on stderr, the frame is counted in `failedFrames`, and the next frame is drawn whole.\n- Fixture `GpuErrorPixels` in `tests/run.sh render`.\n\n**Not found**\n\nWhich canvas in RayDE reached the limit. A tall canvas in a scroller does not (checked to 14523 px), and the Git graph's scene is some thousands of triangles, not millions. Candidates are a minimap of a very large file, a terminal with a long scrollback, or a canvas whose paths are not culled when zoomed far in. With this change the run says so on stderr instead of stopping.\n\n**Follow-ups**\n\n- A canvas builds triangles for all of its ops, whatever is in view; culling by the clip would keep a large canvas small.\n- A canvas's table could be split across textures instead of cut.","files":null}]}